  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "I rewrote the two writable files.\n\n**`registry.mjs`** — `resolveFromRegistry(path, records)` now:\n- Validates `path` (throws `TypeError` for non-string, empty, or non-`/`-prefixed input) before any matching.\n- Scans all records once, collecting the **first** matching static record, the **first** matching dynamic record, and the **first** fallback, then applies precedence: static → dynamic → fallback → `null`. This fixes the old bug where a fallback (or an earlier dynamic) short-circuited the loop before a later static could win.\n- Returns fresh objects (`{ route, params: {} }` / copied params), never mutating or reusing record data.\n\n**`entry.mjs`** — `dispatch(path)` now delegates directly to `resolveFromRegistry(path, defaultRoutes)`, dropping the `legacyResolve` pre-check so `/old/help` is no longer special-cased in the production entry point (it now resolves via the route table, i.e. the fallback). `legacy.mjs` itself is untouched.\n\nUnchanged: `legacy.mjs`, adapters, utils, fixtures, and the route matcher modules (their existing behavior already satisfies the spec: exact static match, segment-wise dynamic match with nonempty values, case-sensitive, trailing-slash distinct).\n\nNot verified by execution — no shell/test runner is available in this environment, so I only reasoned through the logic against `public.test.mjs` expectations (`/users/new` → `user-new`, `/users/Ada` → `user-detail` with `{id:'Ada'}`, `/missing` → `not-found`, `/health?q=one` → `health`, `resolveFromRegistry('/x', [])` → `null`).",
